# Client-side Tor for the reputation-gated egress PoC.
#
# This is the LAPTOP role. Unlike ./torrc (the gateway/droplet role), it does
# NOT publish a hidden service: the client only needs a SOCKS port to dial the
# gateway's .onion through the Tor rendezvous. No onion key is created here.
#
# Distinct ports (9260/9261) so a client Tor can run on the SAME machine as the
# gateway Tor (9250/9251) when simulating the split locally. On a real laptop you
# could instead point the shim at any existing Tor SOCKS (e.g. system tor 9050,
# or Tor Browser 9150) via RGOE_TOR_PORT and skip running this at all.

SocksPort 9260
ControlPort 9261
CookieAuthentication 1

# Client Tor keeps its own state, separate from the gateway's ./tor/data.
DataDirectory ./tor/data-client

Log notice stdout
